# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5.memetic-wikitext" "A numeric entity reads as an entity, and a bare root keeps its intro slash before a fragment or query"

# Two one-token readings. The fragment rule took the `#` of `&#x0001;` for an anchor, painting an entity
# two ways. And the root lookahead that names the slash before `ha.ka.ba` as the root's intro omitted
# `#` and `?`, so `lar:///a.b.c#/slot` read that slash as plain path.

<<^ code=`&#x0001;`>>
#          ^ - entity.name.tag.anchor.memetic-wikitext

x &#x0001; y
#  ^ - entity.name.tag.anchor.memetic-wikitext

x lar:///a.b.c#/slot y
#       ^ punctuation.separator.root.intro.lar.memetic-wikitext

x lar:///a.b.c?q=1 y
#       ^ punctuation.separator.root.intro.lar.memetic-wikitext

# CONTROL: a fragment after a path still reads as an anchor.

x lar:///a.b.c/d#/slot y
#               ^ entity.name.tag.anchor.memetic-wikitext
